 so they wanted to find out whether it  was well they're grateful because  they're happy or are they happy because  they're grateful so they did experiments  be  scientists to find out and and they did  some simple straightforward experiments  they divided groups of people into three  samples at random one lot of people  wrote down all the things that had made  them miserable in the previous week  another lot just wrote down a story from  the previous week and the third group  the gratitude group wrote down what it  made them feel happy and what they felt  grateful for in the previous week and  the people who were recalled things that  had made them happy for which they felt  grateful were measurably happier four  days afterwards the exercise that made  the biggest difference to them was what  they called the gratitude letter where  they asked him to think of someone who'd  helped them in their life who they'd  never properly acknowledged sometimes a  teacher sometimes a family member  write a letter expressing their  gratitude and then go to that person and  read the letter to them and when they  did that these people that were much  happier for at least two months  afterwards so what they showed is that  gratitude is a very simple practice it's  present in every single religious  tradition giving thanks for what we have  and all the blessings in our lives and  in a sense it's obvious that it's  something that people have always done  and it puts you in a flow because if  you're grateful you acknowledge what's  come to you that you give thanks it  continues the flow the opposite of  gratitude is a sense of entitlement or  taking things for granted and it turns  out that people who are grateful a much  more popular with others than people who  take things for granted feel entitled  and complain all the time well that's  not very surprising either but these are  findings of positive psychology in a  sense reinforce the obvious but in the  modern world unless things have the  imprimatur of science the seal of  scientific approval out people don't  take them so seriously  get your tickets for the world's largest  music and philosophy festival at how the  light gets in aaaggghhh
 

